comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-17T19:35:41.682Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete 2986-item all-status corpus and fresh keyword mutation/events/rebuild/contention search found the shipped primitive pm-e200 and reader-versus-writer owner pm-gh1485. This distinct SDK availability escape is in resolveIndexedMutationEvents: a successful rebuild followed by a refused read throws event_index_unavailable instead of falling back to authoritative history. The completed event primitive remains shipped."
  "2026-10-17T19:45:39.023Z","harness:codex","Second independent negative control: with PM_LOCK_WAIT_MS=30000, an optional rebuild configured with zero wait still blocked event availability beyond1500ms because the environment override won. Added maxWaitMs as an additive SDK lock retry ceiling, forwarded as max_wait_ms to extension overrides; optional event repairs cap retries at zero without changing foreground defaults. Authoritative corruption remains surfaced and index/source transitions keep existing cursor semantics."
  "2026-10-17T19:55:39.351Z","harness:codex","Candidate acceptance now preserves valid SDK/CLI event pages across native writer lock contention, PM_LOCK_WAIT_MS=30000, failed cache repair, and post-rebuild refusal. Native SQLite BUSY is transient and does not trigger a rebuild. Existing event_index_unavailable remains stable for untyped authoritative I/O failure; typed malformed-history errors pass through. SDK surface generator recorded the additive maxWaitMs option with an explicit compatibility acknowledgement. Full coverage, linked tests and static gates are the remaining local delivery checks."
